  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** SI-BONE’s commercial momentum is strengthening, fueled by broader surgeon adoption and significant reimbursement wins that are improving procedure economics. Favorable payor decisions, including Medicare updates, alongside new product clearances, are expanding the addressable market and deepening the company’s competitive position. The business is reaching an inflection where sustained demand for its sacropelvic fixation platform is translating into tangible financial maturation, moving from growth-at-all-costs to a more self-funding trajectory.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has credibly delivered on its profitability roadmap, achieving a first full year of positive adjusted earnings and positive free cash flow, and is guiding for further margin expansion. The disciplined build-out of a productive direct sales force and consistent execution on regulatory milestones underscore operational competence. While the analyst consensus is largely constructive with multiple recent upgrades, a lingering sell rating and a recent share-price pullback suggest some market skepticism persists, though the overarching narrative is one of reliable execution and improving financial sustainability.",
